1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:04,300
[♪ opening theme song playing]

2
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:33,970
[KEN] To have a sister
and a best friend

3
00:01:34,050 --> 00:01:35,260
you've trusted your whole life,

4
00:01:35,340 --> 00:01:37,310
and to find out
they're imposters...

5
00:01:38,060 --> 00:01:39,390
If that were me,

6
00:01:39,470 --> 00:01:41,230
I probably wouldn't be able
to leave my room

7
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:42,560
for an entire month.

8
00:01:43,230 --> 00:01:44,190
[HANA] I know, right?

9
00:01:44,900 --> 00:01:47,320
Might be hard to get him
to trust us now, too.

10
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:50,940
Man, I hope not. I don't want
things to be awkward between us.

11
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:53,030
No skin off my back.
I couldn't care less

12
00:01:53,110 --> 00:01:54,530
if this creates
a little distance.

13
00:01:54,610 --> 00:01:56,070
I hate kids.

14
00:01:56,620 --> 00:01:59,200
[KEN] Does that mean
Ms. Hana hates me, too?

15
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:01,120
♪

16
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:03,540
Now, can't allow this
to get cold.

17
00:02:05,880 --> 00:02:07,170
One second.

18
00:02:07,250 --> 00:02:09,460
This should cover food
for this month.

19
00:02:09,550 --> 00:02:11,510
Oh, I almost forgot.

20
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:13,220
Thank you for the offering.

21
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:14,930
Are you sure
you don't need extra

22
00:02:15,010 --> 00:02:16,510
since I'm not paying rent?

23
00:02:16,590 --> 00:02:19,140
You're 13. You're already
helping more than you should.

24
00:02:19,810 --> 00:02:21,430
Actually, on that note,

25
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:23,350
you should probably be
in school.

26
00:02:23,440 --> 00:02:24,640
What's the plan?

27
00:02:24,940 --> 00:02:27,310
Uh, do you need us to
help you transfer to one nearby?

28
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:30,150
Right. Yeah, I guess so.

29
00:02:30,230 --> 00:02:31,780
[Hana moans]

30
00:02:32,570 --> 00:02:33,570
Hm?

31
00:02:34,450 --> 00:02:36,280
Don't wanna do school?

32
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:38,160
[Jiro groans]

33
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:43,870
Do you think that you'd be able
to teach me how to use a weapon?

34
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:46,710
I... want to get stronger.

35
00:02:47,170 --> 00:02:48,210
[HANA] Hm...

36
00:02:48,960 --> 00:02:50,040
[slurping]

37
00:02:51,130 --> 00:02:53,550
Well, if you don't want to,
I won't make you.

38
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,630
Uh, what?

39
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,680
Education's important,
but school isn't the only way.

40
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,470
I'm sure you can learn
without it.

41
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,600
If you talk to people
in my line of work,

42
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:04,680
you'll find lots of them
took shortcuts.

43
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:07,020
[KEN] Uh, is that really okay?

44
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,230
All of us Higashi Village folks
have been ousted from society.

45
00:03:10,310 --> 00:03:12,230
You gotta make do
with what you can get.

46
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,360
Now, come on.

47
00:03:13,440 --> 00:03:15,400
You wanna be stronger,
you gotta eat.

48
00:03:15,490 --> 00:03:18,160
Most fights are won
by bodyweight alone.

49
00:03:20,660 --> 00:03:22,950
Not gonna get big
unless you eat big.

50
00:03:23,790 --> 00:03:24,830
Thanks, Hana.

51
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:25,910
[Jiro whines]

52
00:03:26,460 --> 00:03:28,880
[KEN] You know, I feel like
you're always eating a ton

53
00:03:28,960 --> 00:03:30,540
and yet you're still so small.

54
00:03:30,630 --> 00:03:32,420
[HANA] Yeah, doesn't it suck?

55
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,170
I keep trying to bulk up.

56
00:03:38,430 --> 00:03:39,970
[Asa (fake) breathes nervously]

57
00:03:40,470 --> 00:03:43,350
-Brother--
-Excuse me, what was that?

58
00:03:43,430 --> 00:03:45,430
Who're you calling "brother?"

59
00:03:45,520 --> 00:03:47,480
There's only one person
who gets to call him that,

60
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,810
and that would be me!

61
00:03:48,900 --> 00:03:49,940
[Yuru groans]

62
00:03:50,310 --> 00:03:52,690
Sorry, she's been
calling him that for so long,

63
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:55,240
it's habit.
Please forgive her, Asa.

64
00:03:56,900 --> 00:03:58,160
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
I'm so glad to see

65
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,910
you're all right, partner.

66
00:03:59,990 --> 00:04:01,660
The moment that
I sensed you down here,

67
00:04:01,740 --> 00:04:03,910
I was worried
the worst was gonna happen.

68
00:04:05,410 --> 00:04:07,580
[ASA (FAKE)]
I'm sorry I made you worry.

69
00:04:07,660 --> 00:04:08,830
[cries]

70
00:04:12,460 --> 00:04:14,170
All those years...

71
00:04:14,250 --> 00:04:16,800
they told me that you had
to stay locked in the cage

72
00:04:16,880 --> 00:04:18,340
in order
to keep the village safe.

73
00:04:19,130 --> 00:04:20,680
I thought it was normal,

74
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:22,600
that it's what
the village needed.

75
00:04:23,260 --> 00:04:25,470
I just assumed
that's how it worked

76
00:04:25,560 --> 00:04:27,100
and never thought to doubt it.

77
00:04:27,180 --> 00:04:29,560
Sorry. With a little hindsight,

78
00:04:29,640 --> 00:04:31,770
it obviously
doesn't make any sense.

79
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:36,190
It's insane. Who would keep
a cute little kid in a cell?

80
00:04:36,280 --> 00:04:38,650
Oh, she's cute?
Well, why do you think that is?

81
00:04:38,740 --> 00:04:41,030
It's because
she was copying yours truly.

82
00:04:41,410 --> 00:04:43,410
[BOTH]
Why is she focused on that?

83
00:04:43,780 --> 00:04:44,950
[ASA] Hold the phone!

84
00:04:45,040 --> 00:04:47,200
So you're basically saying
I'm adorable, too!

85
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:48,410
Say it again!

86
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:50,620
No way! Shut your trap.

87
00:04:50,710 --> 00:04:52,710
There's no need to hide
how much you love me!

88
00:04:52,790 --> 00:04:54,500
Give your cute little sister
a hug!

89
00:04:54,590 --> 00:04:57,510
Gods, you know you're a real
pain in the butt sometimes?

90
00:04:57,590 --> 00:04:59,840
Hmm, I'm so sorry.

91
00:04:59,930 --> 00:05:01,470
I shouldn't have lied
to my brother.

92
00:05:01,550 --> 00:05:03,350
He's not your brother.

93
00:05:03,430 --> 00:05:04,970
[ASA (FAKE)] I'm sorry,
please, I'm so sorry!

94
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:07,140
So what do you want me
to call you,

95
00:05:07,220 --> 00:05:08,520
if "brother" doesn't work?

96
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:10,390
Uh, just "Yuru" should be fine.

97
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:15,190
[ASA (FAKE)] I'm sorry
for deceiving you, really.

98
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:18,400
For keeping you chained
to the village.

99
00:05:18,990 --> 00:05:22,400
It was wrong. I knew that,
but I kept doing it.

100
00:05:23,910 --> 00:05:26,200
You were always so nice to me.

101
00:05:26,950 --> 00:05:31,160
You came to visit me every day.
We'd talk about everything.

102
00:05:32,330 --> 00:05:33,540
I loved it so.

103
00:05:33,630 --> 00:05:35,580
[cries]

104
00:05:37,130 --> 00:05:39,840
I wished life would
never have to change.

105
00:05:39,920 --> 00:05:43,050
Forever and ever,

106
00:05:43,130 --> 00:05:45,640
I wanted
to keep being your sister.

107
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,600
[cries]

108
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:49,430
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

109
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:52,140
I'm sorry.

110
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,110
[YURU] There's no need for you
to copy her anymore.

111
00:05:59,730 --> 00:06:01,650
I would like to see
who you really are.

112
00:06:01,740 --> 00:06:03,070
[ASA (FAKE)] Huh?

113
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:12,200
[whimpers]

114
00:06:13,330 --> 00:06:15,750
Uh? So tiny.

115
00:06:15,830 --> 00:06:17,960
[chuckles] You're even smaller.

116
00:06:18,040 --> 00:06:20,170
Tell me, what's your name?

117
00:06:20,250 --> 00:06:21,590
What do you mean?

118
00:06:21,670 --> 00:06:23,970
Ms. Kyoka must've called you
something, didn't she?

119
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,510
Kiri.

120
00:06:27,350 --> 00:06:29,640
She named me
after the pretty flowers

121
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:32,230
that bloom
on the village's mountain.

122
00:06:32,890 --> 00:06:34,020
"Kiri."

123
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,850
That's a good name.

124
00:06:35,940 --> 00:06:38,360
And she said "Danji's" fitting
for a masculine son,

125
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:39,480
just like me!

126
00:06:39,570 --> 00:06:42,150
Well, yeah. It means "boy."

127
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,990
-So you ready?
-[KIRI] Mm.

128
00:06:44,070 --> 00:06:45,780
We'll tell you the truth.

129
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:47,990
At least everything we know.

130
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:49,450
[bird screeching]

131
00:06:49,530 --> 00:06:51,120
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
A long time ago,

132
00:06:51,200 --> 00:06:53,290
Higashi was a stronghold.

133
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:55,370
There were smaller castles
around it,

134
00:06:55,460 --> 00:06:57,500
each one with a village
of its own.

135
00:06:58,630 --> 00:07:00,000
In one of those hamlets,

136
00:07:00,090 --> 00:07:01,800
we were
the local Zashiki-Warashi,

137
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:03,760
enshrined to bring them
good luck.

138
00:07:04,550 --> 00:07:06,590
We passed between a few masters,

139
00:07:06,680 --> 00:07:09,430
but they were all simple
and real kind.

140
00:07:09,510 --> 00:07:10,600
♪

141
00:07:11,010 --> 00:07:14,640
Though small, that village
held nothing but our love.

142
00:07:14,940 --> 00:07:16,940
They say some divine daemons
called Left and Right

143
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:17,980
live up there!

144
00:07:18,060 --> 00:07:21,020
[KIRI] Oh, yes?
I wanna meet them.

145
00:07:22,360 --> 00:07:24,150
[MAN 1] A big war's brewing.

146
00:07:24,240 --> 00:07:27,150
I hear the lord of Higashi
went into battle himself!

147
00:07:27,240 --> 00:07:28,780
[WOMAN]
But who are they against?

148
00:07:28,870 --> 00:07:30,120
[MAN 2] We've been
ordered to send

149
00:07:30,200 --> 00:07:31,870
some of our strongest young men.

150
00:07:31,950 --> 00:07:34,200
They said they need
more fighters.

151
00:07:34,290 --> 00:07:35,620
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] That was
the first time we heard

152
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:36,870
about that war.

153
00:07:36,960 --> 00:07:39,170
It must have been about
400 years ago.

154
00:07:39,250 --> 00:07:41,130
Kids, great news.

155
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:44,170
I've been chosen to go to war
alongside the lord of our land.

156
00:07:44,250 --> 00:07:46,170
I'll make sure
to do you two proud

157
00:07:46,260 --> 00:07:47,930
and come back
with heaps of riches.

158
00:07:48,010 --> 00:07:49,760
We wanna go wherever you go.

159
00:07:49,840 --> 00:07:51,050
We can be helpful.

160
00:07:51,140 --> 00:07:52,890
Oh, I appreciate the thought,

161
00:07:52,970 --> 00:07:55,480
but war is too dangerous
for the likes of you.

162
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:58,190
-[KIRI] Aw...
-But we would like to come, too.

163
00:07:59,100 --> 00:08:01,480
[MASTER] I'll be fine,
but if anything did happen,

164
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,320
you'd become stray daemons.

165
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,980
So let's end our contract.

166
00:08:05,070 --> 00:08:06,740
And you can wait for me
as relics.

167
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,860
Then we'll start a new contract

168
00:08:08,950 --> 00:08:11,530
as soon as I get back.
How about it?

169
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:13,450
Would you two become
my daemons again?

170
00:08:13,540 --> 00:08:14,950
Of course we will!

171
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:18,250
I can hardly wait!
Come back with stories!

172
00:08:18,330 --> 00:08:19,540
♪

173
00:08:20,210 --> 00:08:22,210
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
So we returned to relics

174
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:24,340
and waited patiently
in our box,

175
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,010
until our master
would come home.

176
00:08:28,930 --> 00:08:32,640
Eventually, we heard
through passersby

177
00:08:32,720 --> 00:08:34,640
that the war was over.

178
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:37,140
In the end, the East prevailed.

179
00:08:37,230 --> 00:08:40,770
[ASA] A war 400 years ago
that the East won.

180
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:43,860
-The Battle of Sekigahara?
-[BOTH] Mm?

181
00:08:43,940 --> 00:08:45,730
Wait, you've heard
about this fight?

182
00:08:45,820 --> 00:08:47,780
Is "Sekigahara"
what they call it here?

183
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:49,900
Yeah. It was a historic battle

184
00:08:49,990 --> 00:08:51,910
that happened right around
the time you said.

185
00:08:51,990 --> 00:08:53,280
Whoa. Really?

186
00:08:53,370 --> 00:08:55,830
The Tokugawa shogunate
ruled the land after that.

187
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:58,040
They held power for 200 years.

188
00:08:58,120 --> 00:09:00,250
You said the lord of Higashi
at the time

189
00:09:00,330 --> 00:09:01,580
was fighting in that war.

190
00:09:01,670 --> 00:09:03,710
I've never even heard
someone mention that.

191
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:05,790
Seems strange
that it's not a bigger part

192
00:09:05,880 --> 00:09:07,840
of the village's history
if he won.

193
00:09:08,470 --> 00:09:10,090
We never heard anything either.

194
00:09:10,170 --> 00:09:11,260
You're right,

195
00:09:11,550 --> 00:09:13,850
not even about any lands
he won for the village.

196
00:09:14,970 --> 00:09:17,100
Maybe he did something
bad enough to be taboo.

197
00:09:17,180 --> 00:09:18,060
[both gasp]

198
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:19,480
[ASA] Now that's been said,

199
00:09:19,560 --> 00:09:23,100
maybe it was nothing
and he just wasn't noteworthy.

200
00:09:23,190 --> 00:09:25,570
What did your previous master
tell you?

201
00:09:25,650 --> 00:09:28,070
He must have known
since he went to war.

202
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,070
Did he mention it?

203
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,150
[BOTH] Mm...

204
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:35,530
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
Our old master never came home.

205
00:09:35,620 --> 00:09:36,530
[BOTH] Uh?

206
00:09:37,370 --> 00:09:39,120
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] We wanted to
renew our contract with him

207
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:41,160
like we said, so we waited...

208
00:09:41,660 --> 00:09:43,500
And waited...

209
00:09:43,960 --> 00:09:46,590
And waited, and waited.

210
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:51,590
Over time, the voices
around us began to fade.

211
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:54,720
We knew we had been forgotten.

212
00:09:54,800 --> 00:09:55,850
♪

213
00:09:56,390 --> 00:09:58,390
Our little hamlet was gone.

214
00:09:58,470 --> 00:10:00,480
Everyone had abandoned it.

215
00:10:00,560 --> 00:10:03,230
- [footsteps]
- As the years wasted away,

216
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,900
we thought we'd waste away
with them,

217
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:09,110
never to form a contract
with a human again,

218
00:10:09,190 --> 00:10:10,650
until one day...

219
00:10:10,740 --> 00:10:14,360
[MAN] Oh, there you are.
The legend was true.

220
00:10:14,450 --> 00:10:16,530
Must've been lonely in there.

221
00:10:16,990 --> 00:10:18,200
Come with me.

222
00:10:19,330 --> 00:10:20,330
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
A kind young man

223
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:23,870
heard a legend about
some Zashiki-Warashi in the area

224
00:10:23,960 --> 00:10:26,330
and followed it
until he tracked us down.

225
00:10:27,210 --> 00:10:28,380
You know him.

226
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:30,710
The Higashi Village retainer,
Roei.

227
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:33,760
Hey, I do know that name.
That's the previous Tadera!

228
00:10:33,840 --> 00:10:36,300
Uh-huh. Also Dera's pa.

229
00:10:36,390 --> 00:10:37,890
Oh, so they're related?

230
00:10:37,970 --> 00:10:41,890
Mr. Roei took us straight to
our new home in Higashi Village.

231
00:10:42,600 --> 00:10:44,020
That's where we met her,

232
00:10:44,100 --> 00:10:47,190
who we call "Ma,"
our master, Kyoka.

233
00:10:48,110 --> 00:10:50,480
She'd lost both her husband
and her two children

234
00:10:50,570 --> 00:10:52,360
in a terrible landslide.

235
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,780
She couldn't even
get out of bed.

236
00:10:55,860 --> 00:10:57,450
In some small way,

237
00:10:57,530 --> 00:11:00,200
Roei wanted to help
fill the hole in her heart.

238
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,950
He brought us together

239
00:11:02,040 --> 00:11:05,080
and instructed her on how
to form a contract with us.

240
00:11:05,160 --> 00:11:06,330
♪

241
00:11:15,170 --> 00:11:16,970
You must be our new master!

242
00:11:17,050 --> 00:11:18,300
You should give us names,

243
00:11:18,390 --> 00:11:21,310
-whatever you think fits.
-Uh? Uh...

244
00:11:21,390 --> 00:11:23,980
Tell me, I've heard stories,

245
00:11:24,060 --> 00:11:26,060
but are these kids
what they call daemons?

246
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:27,100
[ROEI] Yep.

247
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,190
I thought they were legends
for children.

248
00:11:30,150 --> 00:11:31,610
Do you want to play with us?

249
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:33,940
We're gonna stay
by your side forever and a day.

250
00:11:34,780 --> 00:11:36,320
[BOTH] Master.

251
00:11:36,610 --> 00:11:37,950
[chuckles]

252
00:11:41,280 --> 00:11:42,740
Thank you, dears.

253
00:11:43,490 --> 00:11:46,660
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
She seemed sad, but also happy.

254
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:50,290
[YAMAHA]
Oh, my, those are daemons.

255
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:52,590
Some Zashiki-Warashi?

256
00:11:52,670 --> 00:11:54,590
They'll bring you good fortune.

257
00:11:54,670 --> 00:11:57,340
Say, Kyoka,
once you're feeling well enough

258
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:58,800
to be back on your feet,

259
00:11:58,880 --> 00:12:01,350
I'd like you to come
to the keep and work for me.

260
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:03,180
So that old lady,

261
00:12:03,260 --> 00:12:05,730
she could see us
without us having to let her.

262
00:12:05,810 --> 00:12:07,480
Is she a Daemon Wielder, too?

263
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:10,690
Uh, could most people
not see these two?

264
00:12:11,020 --> 00:12:12,570
[ROEI] Only Daemon Wielders,

265
00:12:12,650 --> 00:12:15,400
anyone who the daemons choose
to reveal themselves to,

266
00:12:15,490 --> 00:12:18,320
and a few others who just happen
to have the sense.

267
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,990
Me, for instance?

268
00:12:20,070 --> 00:12:21,820
I've got my own pair
down the mountain.

269
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:24,330
Who was that old lady, master?

270
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:27,910
That's Granny Yamaha,
the leader of the village.

271
00:12:29,410 --> 00:12:31,960
She's the oldest person
here by far.

272
00:12:32,040 --> 00:12:35,300
She claims not even she
can remember how old she is.

273
00:12:40,090 --> 00:12:42,300
-[wind howling]
-[bird cawing]

274
00:12:45,060 --> 00:12:46,600
[breathes heavily]

275
00:12:46,680 --> 00:12:49,020
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] A short time
after Ma started at the keep,

276
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:51,770
an outsider wandered
into the village.

277
00:12:51,850 --> 00:12:53,940
Her name was Nagisa.

278
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,610
[breathes heavily]

279
00:12:57,570 --> 00:12:58,780
[cow moos]

280
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,490
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
The way she dressed...

281
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:03,280
It was nothing like
what we wore in the mountains.

282
00:13:03,370 --> 00:13:05,910
That's how we knew she was
from the modern world.

283
00:13:05,990 --> 00:13:07,330
[Nagisa panting]

284
00:13:08,330 --> 00:13:09,330
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
When they told her

285
00:13:09,410 --> 00:13:10,620
she couldn't leave,

286
00:13:10,710 --> 00:13:12,750
she became horribly depressed.

287
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:16,210
Mr. Mine felt sorry for her

288
00:13:16,290 --> 00:13:18,300
and did everything
he could to help.

289
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,090
[MINE] Miss Nagisa?

290
00:13:20,170 --> 00:13:21,470
[Nagisa yelps]

291
00:13:21,550 --> 00:13:23,970
I thought we could
have some boar stew.

292
00:13:24,050 --> 00:13:25,600
It'll cheer you up.

293
00:13:25,680 --> 00:13:27,260
[Nagisa breathes uneasily]

294
00:13:27,350 --> 00:13:29,560
[NAGISA] Wow, that is so grody.

295
00:13:29,640 --> 00:13:31,350
So what? "Grody?"

296
00:13:31,440 --> 00:13:34,060
[Nagisa laughs]

297
00:13:34,150 --> 00:13:36,270
Never mind. And you know what?

298
00:13:36,360 --> 00:13:38,110
I do feel a little better now.

299
00:13:39,030 --> 00:13:40,450
[laughs]

300
00:13:40,530 --> 00:13:42,280
[both chuckle]

301
00:13:42,360 --> 00:13:43,740
♪

302
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:51,870
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
Later, Yuru and Asa were born.

303
00:13:53,500 --> 00:13:56,750
And something
in the villagers' eyes changed.

304
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:59,250
Because we didn't come
from there,

305
00:13:59,340 --> 00:14:01,800
we didn't know
Higashi's whole history.

306
00:14:02,590 --> 00:14:04,260
Of course, we heard legends...

307
00:14:05,510 --> 00:14:07,470
...about the Break
and Seal twins. But...

308
00:14:08,140 --> 00:14:09,220
[Kyoka grunts]

309
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,810
In the face
of unimaginable power,

310
00:14:11,890 --> 00:14:13,730
people lose their humanity.

311
00:14:14,390 --> 00:14:15,650
[DANJI (TSUGAI)] We could tell

312
00:14:15,730 --> 00:14:18,020
Ma had pretty serious opinions
about it,

313
00:14:18,110 --> 00:14:20,230
but she never went into detail.

314
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:22,320
[rustling]

315
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:24,990
[chirping]

316
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:26,660
[AZAMI'S MOM] Seal's here.

317
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,490
Break, too.

318
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:30,290
What's taking the bandits
so long?

319
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:31,540
They should hurry.

320
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,710
How long must we wait

321
00:14:32,790 --> 00:14:34,660
until Higashi Village
reigns supreme?

322
00:14:34,750 --> 00:14:38,500
Hey, Mommy?
What are you talking about?

323
00:14:38,590 --> 00:14:41,210
Nothing, Azami.
Go back to sleep.

324
00:14:41,300 --> 00:14:42,550
♪

325
00:14:44,260 --> 00:14:45,430
[Danji (younger) sighs]

326
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:46,590
-[hoofbeats]
-[gasps]

327
00:14:46,680 --> 00:14:48,600
-Yuru!
-Mm?

328
00:14:48,680 --> 00:14:51,390
Are you going out hunting?
I'll join!

329
00:14:51,470 --> 00:14:53,850
I'm fine, Danji.
Don't follow me.

330
00:14:53,930 --> 00:14:56,980
But it's dangerous going into
the mountains all by yourself!

331
00:14:57,060 --> 00:14:58,730
[YURU] You're just trying
to slack off your work

332
00:14:58,820 --> 00:14:59,770
in the fields!

333
00:14:59,860 --> 00:15:01,190
[DANJI] Aw, you got me.

334
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,240
DANJI (TSUGAI) After that,
you know everything.

335
00:15:04,740 --> 00:15:06,780
Our ma got an order
from Granny Yamaha.

336
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:09,120
She needed Kiri
to impersonate Asa.

337
00:15:10,280 --> 00:15:11,540
But that wasn't all.

338
00:15:11,620 --> 00:15:13,370
Ma told me to watch over you

339
00:15:13,450 --> 00:15:15,540
and to make sure Granny
never found out.

340
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:17,080
[Yuru grunts]

341
00:15:18,630 --> 00:15:21,920
If you don't mind, I'd like
to send you out there before us.

342
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,090
I want to chat
with my sister in private.

343
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:25,550
[Asa gasps] By ourselves?

344
00:15:26,590 --> 00:15:29,140
Our first heart-to-heart
since we were kids!

345
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,600
Could you quit being weird
and kick these two out?

346
00:15:31,680 --> 00:15:34,390
Hey, Yin and Yang?
Let the Zashiki-Warashi out,

347
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:36,140
but keep my brother and me here!

348
00:15:36,230 --> 00:15:37,520
[DANJI (TSUGAI)]
Yuru, one thing.

349
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:39,190
I know you're mad at your sister

350
00:15:39,270 --> 00:15:40,980
for attacking
the village that day,

351
00:15:41,070 --> 00:15:42,980
but she didn't actually
kill anyone herself.

352
00:15:44,070 --> 00:15:46,200
Our ma got bruised up
by some rubble,

353
00:15:46,280 --> 00:15:48,610
but that was the worst thing
she did to any of the villagers!

354
00:15:51,490 --> 00:15:52,530
[Yuru grunts]

355
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:55,120
Don't let him make you think
I'm a saint.

356
00:15:56,410 --> 00:15:58,120
The only reason
I didn't kill anyone

357
00:15:58,210 --> 00:15:59,670
is 'cause I didn't have to.

358
00:15:59,750 --> 00:16:02,340
If I even suspect
someone's a threat to the people

359
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:05,380
who are important to me,
I'll show no mercy.

360
00:16:07,510 --> 00:16:10,050
You know,
you haven't lied to me once

361
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:13,100
since we were reunited,
and I want to acknowledge that.

362
00:16:13,180 --> 00:16:15,850
There were some things
that must've been hard to say,

363
00:16:15,930 --> 00:16:18,020
but you were still
perfectly honest.

364
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:20,560
[ASA] I'm sorry, Yuru.

365
00:16:20,650 --> 00:16:21,980
You said you were looking

366
00:16:22,060 --> 00:16:23,900
for the innocent little sister
you knew.

367
00:16:23,980 --> 00:16:26,030
I'm afraid
you'll never find her.

368
00:16:26,860 --> 00:16:28,070
No.

369
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:30,410
She died that day.

370
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:34,740
So now, I wanna be honest
about how I feel, too.

371
00:16:35,290 --> 00:16:36,660
In those 10 years

372
00:16:36,750 --> 00:16:39,410
after our parents
fled the village, I struggled.

373
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,960
Danji and Kiri were my rocks
during that period.

374
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:44,630
They were my reason to live.

375
00:16:45,380 --> 00:16:47,260
Whenever the weight
of being abandoned

376
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:48,550
felt like too much,

377
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:50,720
I had a sister and a best friend
to lean on.

378
00:16:50,800 --> 00:16:53,890
Has that changed?
Now that I know they were fakes?

379
00:16:53,970 --> 00:16:55,720
Does that mean
the strength they gave me

380
00:16:55,810 --> 00:16:56,890
wasn't real, either?

381
00:16:57,890 --> 00:16:59,310
I think it was real,

382
00:16:59,390 --> 00:17:01,480
so I can't find it in me
to hate them.

383
00:17:02,480 --> 00:17:03,400
[ASA] Hm.

384
00:17:04,690 --> 00:17:05,900
-[exclaims]
-Huh?

385
00:17:05,980 --> 00:17:08,400
Aw, man! This is so unfair!

386
00:17:09,030 --> 00:17:12,200
I only got to spend six years
with you before I left.

387
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,410
How am I supposed
to compare to their 10?

388
00:17:14,490 --> 00:17:15,830
And it gets even worse

389
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:18,040
when you consider we were babies
for part of that.

390
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:20,080
If we're only counting the years
we actually remember,

391
00:17:20,160 --> 00:17:23,170
then we're looking at three,
maybe four at best.

392
00:17:23,250 --> 00:17:24,460
[sighs]

393
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:28,300
It isn't fair.

394
00:17:29,010 --> 00:17:30,510
♪

395
00:17:32,470 --> 00:17:33,640
[Yuru sighs]

396
00:17:35,050 --> 00:17:37,220
Well, now we're together again,
aren't we?

397
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:38,970
Anything you wanna do?

398
00:17:39,470 --> 00:17:40,980
Like, right now?

399
00:17:41,060 --> 00:17:42,850
No, like dreams for the future.

400
00:17:42,940 --> 00:17:45,940
Oh, yeah!
I really wanna go to Disney!

401
00:17:46,020 --> 00:17:47,780
To what? Dizzy?

402
00:17:47,860 --> 00:17:50,150
I wanna buy tons
of cute stuffed animals,

403
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:51,740
enjoy all the rides and parades,

404
00:17:51,820 --> 00:17:53,450
and take a picture
at Cinderella's castle...

405
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,450
[YURU] A castle?
So there's a lord?

406
00:17:55,530 --> 00:17:57,290
Wonder what
the crop yield's like.

407
00:17:57,740 --> 00:17:58,830
[Asa sighs]

408
00:17:58,910 --> 00:18:01,200
I want to have fun
doing normal things.

409
00:18:01,290 --> 00:18:02,460
Attend some school

410
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:04,750
and whine about studying
like a normal kid.

411
00:18:04,830 --> 00:18:07,880
Talk about the hot boys
in class like a normal girl.

412
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,590
Complain about my boring job

413
00:18:09,670 --> 00:18:11,720
on the commuter train
like a normal adult.

414
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:12,970
That's all.

415
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:15,390
I just want a normal life.

416
00:18:16,350 --> 00:18:17,850
Good joke, right?

417
00:18:17,930 --> 00:18:19,310
Like any of that's possible

418
00:18:19,390 --> 00:18:21,470
in this kill or be killed
world we're in.

419
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:24,940
[YURU] When you think about
having this normal life,

420
00:18:25,560 --> 00:18:27,480
are Mom, Dad, and I
a part of it?

421
00:18:27,570 --> 00:18:28,820
Yeah!

422
00:18:28,900 --> 00:18:30,610
Then we need
to build it together,

423
00:18:30,690 --> 00:18:32,280
even if it takes us years.

424
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:35,070
We had 10 apart,
so what's 10 more?

425
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:36,870
We'll defeat all our enemies,

426
00:18:37,910 --> 00:18:39,790
reunite with our mom and dad,

427
00:18:39,870 --> 00:18:42,950
and live a life together
without needing to hide.

428
00:18:43,040 --> 00:18:45,330
And that place... Diz-ay?

429
00:18:45,420 --> 00:18:47,210
We'll go as a family!

430
00:18:47,290 --> 00:18:48,880
We'll have fun at the castle!

431
00:18:48,960 --> 00:18:50,090
Right!

432
00:18:50,170 --> 00:18:52,590
And I learned something
you should know

433
00:18:52,670 --> 00:18:53,970
about our parents.

434
00:18:54,050 --> 00:18:55,300
Years ago,

435
00:18:55,380 --> 00:18:57,050
someone had to teach Mom and Dad

436
00:18:57,140 --> 00:18:59,560
how to get through the barrier
and escape from Higashi.

437
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:00,640
It was Roei.

438
00:19:00,720 --> 00:19:03,270
Mm? So Dera's father
helped them?

439
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,940
Seriously? Mom and Dad
never mentioned

440
00:19:06,020 --> 00:19:07,400
a word about him to me.

441
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:09,520
-Likely for his sake.
-Uh?

442
00:19:09,610 --> 00:19:12,570
What he did was considered
a betrayal of Higashi.

443
00:19:13,190 --> 00:19:15,610
So to repay him,
they chose to keep quiet.

444
00:19:15,700 --> 00:19:17,410
Even to their own family.

445
00:19:18,490 --> 00:19:20,030
It's not just Dera.

446
00:19:20,120 --> 00:19:22,120
Roei has another son
down the mountain.

447
00:19:22,620 --> 00:19:25,410
But neither of them
have any idea where he could be.

448
00:19:26,330 --> 00:19:29,420
If there's any chance Roei still
has contact with our parents,

449
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:31,420
then tracking him down
may be our best lead.

450
00:19:31,500 --> 00:19:32,670
[ASA] Mm.

451
00:19:33,050 --> 00:19:35,590
You can count on Dera and me
to hunt his old man down.

452
00:19:35,670 --> 00:19:37,180
Cool. Thank you for that.

453
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:41,510
Also, there's a Daemon Wielder
with katanas.

454
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:44,350
He claims to know what happened
to our parents

455
00:19:44,430 --> 00:19:46,270
-when they disappeared.
-[gasps softly]

456
00:19:46,850 --> 00:19:48,310
[ASA] Katanas?

457
00:19:49,480 --> 00:19:53,230
[gasps] Ivan Yosano!
What did he say to you?

458
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:54,860
Our parents, where are they at?

459
00:19:54,940 --> 00:19:57,950
-What does he know?
-Listen to me carefully, Asa.

460
00:19:58,030 --> 00:19:59,240
Try not to panic.

461
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:03,240
He told me...
he killed Mom and Dad.

462
00:20:03,330 --> 00:20:05,830
Ivan claimed he used the swords
he was wielding

463
00:20:05,910 --> 00:20:07,160
to cut them both down.

464
00:20:07,250 --> 00:20:09,420
-[breathing heavily]
-We wanted to ask more,

465
00:20:09,500 --> 00:20:11,290
but he escaped before we could.

466
00:20:12,090 --> 00:20:14,550
[continues breathing heavily]

467
00:20:17,380 --> 00:20:18,630
Asa!

468
00:20:20,430 --> 00:20:23,510
-Listen!
-No way. He killed them?

469
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:25,140
Calm down, Asa, please!

470
00:20:25,220 --> 00:20:28,640
[tearfully]
Mom and Dad, they're really...

471
00:20:29,690 --> 00:20:31,150
This is my fault.

472
00:20:31,230 --> 00:20:34,020
It's because they took me away
from the village.

473
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:36,990
They were dragged into this
'cause I was born.

474
00:20:37,070 --> 00:20:38,570
Asa, focus!

475
00:20:38,650 --> 00:20:40,990
Just because he said it
doesn't mean that it's true!

476
00:20:41,070 --> 00:20:42,580
You can't believe him.

477
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:45,370
The whole world is filled
with people you shouldn't trust.

478
00:20:45,450 --> 00:20:47,910
Don't believe it until you've
seen it with your own eyes.

479
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,790
You said yourself that
Mom and Dad were alive and well!

480
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,380
You believed that!

481
00:20:53,130 --> 00:20:56,710
Just breathe... Exhale slowly.

482
00:20:58,420 --> 00:20:59,550
[exhales]

483
00:21:02,760 --> 00:21:04,510
What was I thinking?

484
00:21:04,930 --> 00:21:06,850
They've gotta be out there,
somewhere.

485
00:21:06,930 --> 00:21:10,100
That's right. And if anyone's
trying to hold them captive,

486
00:21:10,190 --> 00:21:13,060
we'll just bust them out!
Then we'll go.

487
00:21:14,150 --> 00:21:18,280
The four of us.
Live a happy and normal life!

488
00:21:23,660 --> 00:21:25,870
We'll start with those katanas.

489
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:29,580
I'll use Break to dissolve
their contract with him.

490
00:21:30,210 --> 00:21:33,250
And Yuru...
Next time you find him,

491
00:21:33,330 --> 00:21:35,710
do whatever you can
to lure him towards me.

492
00:21:36,710 --> 00:21:39,090
It doesn't matter
how far away he is.

493
00:21:39,170 --> 00:21:42,130
Soon as he enters my sight,
he's done for.

494
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:43,430
[YURU] Good.

495
00:21:43,970 --> 00:21:45,720
Left and Right
are already familiar

496
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:47,390
with the scent of his blood.

497
00:21:47,470 --> 00:21:50,140
We'll lure, but we'll leave
the real hunt to you!

498
00:21:50,230 --> 00:21:51,270
[ASA] Hm.

499
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:57,400
[♪ closing theme song playing]

500
00:23:28,450 --> 00:23:30,120
[GONZO] Good evening, ma'am.

501
00:23:30,830 --> 00:23:31,990
[NATSUKI] Destroyed?

502
00:23:32,330 --> 00:23:34,410
[AKIO] I didn't understand
the pain of others.

503
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:36,920
I felt an emotion
I'd never felt before.
